# Playback header forwarding — libmpv integration

- Date: 2026-11-10
- Machine: macOS 27.0.1 (26A434), darwin/arm64, Apple M3, 8 GiB
- Go: 1.27.3
- MyGo: 0.8.3
- libmpv runtime: vegidio/binaries-mpv 26.10.1, mpv 0.41.0, client API 2.5
- Runtime path: /private/tmp/mumu-runtime/lib

## Command

```sh
CGO_ENABLED=0 go test -tags mumu_mpv -c -o /tmp/mumu-libmpv.test \
  ./internal/player/libmpv
DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/private/tmp/mumu-runtime/lib MUMU_MPV_HEADER_TEST=1 \
  /tmp/mumu-libmpv.test -test.run TestIntegrationPlaybackHeaders -test.v
```

## Observed

```text
=== RUN   TestIntegrationPlaybackHeaders
--- PASS: TestIntegrationPlaybackHeaders (0.30s)
PASS
```

The test serves a synthetic HLS manifest from a local HTTP server and fails
unless:

- `User-Agent` equals `mumu-header-test/0.1`;
- `Referer` equals `https://example.com/watch`;
- a `Cookie` header present in `player.Source.Headers` never reaches the server.

A direct `go test` invocation in this shell failed to `dlopen` libmpv; the
built test binary above is the recorded run. This proves header forwarding for
`http` only. It does not prove `https`, other schemes, renderer behavior or
packaging.
